{"text": "The graph above shows the numbers of very hot days, defined as days with the highest daytime temperature reaching 35˚C or above, in six cities in 2023 and in 2024. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Among the six cities, Cairo showed a greater number of very hot days than any other city in 2023 and in 2024, respectively. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Beijing was the only city whose number of very hot days in 2024 was smaller than that in 2023 among the cities shown in the graph. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In 2024, the number of very hot days in Manila was greater than that in Rome. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Santiago had the smallest number of very hot days in 2023 as well as in 2024 among the cities above. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In Washington, D, C, the number of very hot days in 2024 was more than three times that in 2023.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "g", "r", "a", "p", "h", " ", "a", "b", "o", "v", "e", " ", "s", "h", "o", "w", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "n", "u", "m", "b", "e", "r", "s", " ", "o", "f", " ", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "h", "o", "t", " ", "d", "a", "y", "s", ",", " ", "d", "e", "f", "i", "n", "e", "d", " ", "a", "s", " ", "d", "a", "y", "s", " ", "w", "i", "t", "h", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "h", "i", "g", "h", "e", "s", "t", " ", "d", "a", "y", "t", "i", "m", "e", " ", "t", "e", "m", "p", "e", "r", "a", "t", "u", "r", "e", " ", "r", "e", "a", "c", "h", "i", "n", "g", " ", "3", "5", "˚", "C", " ", "o", "r", " ", "a", "b", "o", "v", "e", ",", " ", "i", "n", " ", "s", "i", "x", " ", "c", "i", "t", "i", "e", "s", " ", "i", "n", " ", "2", "0", "2", "3", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "i", "n", " ", "2", "0", "2", "4", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "A", "m", "o", "n", "g", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "i", "x", " ", "c", "i", "t", "i", "e", "s", ",", " ", "C", "a", "i", "r", "o", " ", "s", "h", "o", "w", "e", "d", " ", "a", " ", "g", "r", "e", "a", "t", "e